# (H-A), finite range `73 ≤ j ≤ 812`: the arithmetic floor on the diagonal, from lower endpoints

Flint's (H-A) export (GPP-bridge `work/flint/ha_dyadic_export_2026_11_16.json`, bridge `c3c80df`) gives,
for `j = 73 … 812`, a rigorous rational ball `[cen − rad, cen + rad] / 2¹⁶⁰` around the diagonal entry
`A_jj` of the run-16 matrix `S_Z^eff` (`L = 0.5`). This file is the kernel half of that check: with
`aLo j = (cen_j − rad_j) / 2¹⁶⁰` it proves

  `c_A · log (4π j) / (4π j)⁴ ≤ a`   whenever   `aLo j ≤ a`,   `c_A = 867483 / 500000`,

for every `j ∈ [73, 812]`. The enclosures are: `π ∈ (3.14159265358979323846, 3.14159265358979323847)`
(Mathlib `Real.pi_gt_d20`/`pi_lt_d20`), `log 2 < 0.6931471808` (`Real.log_two_lt_d9`), and for
`log (4π j) ≤ log W`, `W = 4 π_hi j = 2ᵐ (1 − x)` with `m = ⌊log₂ ⌊W⌋⌋ + 1` and `0 ≤ x ≤ 1/2`
(a rational check), `log (1 − x) ≤ −Σ_{i<24} x^{i+1}/(i+1) + 2⁻²⁴` (Mathlib
`Real.abs_log_sub_add_sum_range_le`). The finite check `haOK_all` is `decide +kernel` over `ℚ`.
The tightest `j` is `74` (relative slack `4.8 · 10⁻⁷`).

**Scope.** This is *only* the implication "named lower endpoint `≤ A_jj` ⇒ floor". Not in this file and not
